From: Resonate web port <dave.torosyan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:28:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Recognize octave bass clefs; use octave clefs when the 8
 is there

Vocal scores for low voices write the bass part with a bass clef that has
a small 8 below (sounding an octave lower), e.g. Hades in "Hey, Little
Songbird". F_CLEF_8VA/8VB were left out of the clefs looked for at the
start of a staff ("reported to be extremely rare"), so such a part came
out an octave too high.

- F_CLEF_8VA and F_CLEF_8VB are now header clef candidates.
- The classifier is weak on octave clefs: on a bass clef with an 8 below,
  the plain clef alone grades ~0.8 and the clef + 8 glyph as F_CLEF_8VB
  only 0.05-0.3, so the plain clef always won. But octave candidates only
  show up when the 8 is there (none on 22 plain bass clefs of a piano
  score). So when the classifier proposes the octave variant of the chosen
  G or F clef for a glyph extending past it by at least half an interline
  (below for 8vb, above for 8va), that variant is used, with the plain
  clef's grade. Logged as "Staff#N F_CLEF_8VB with an 8 below".

Test scan: 20 of 21 low-voice staves now get F_CLEF_8VB (the last one's 8
touches the system barline). Other test scores: identical output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
